  "body": "## What and why\n\nComplete the remaining documentation requested in #962. All prerequisite PRs are merged.\nThe original operation-order rows already shipped in #1161.\n\n- Add `set_units { \"unit\": \"mm\" | \"inch\" }`, its undo/redo rule and its refusals.\n- Remove `SetUnits` from the remaining gaps and list it as shipped.\n- Add `import_model.facet_budget`, its current default, re-import rule and readback.\n- Add `get_job.units`, `machine {path, definition}` and setup `post` / `posts_with`.\n- Keep the existing rename/reorder, edit_tool, pick_in_box, WCS, coolant, edit_machine and set_setup_post rows unchanged.\n- Add four focused documentation tests beside the existing skill tests.\n\nNo Rust behavior, NC output, dependency, workflow or release file changes.\nThe decision is in `docs/decisions/962-mcp-skill-remainder.md`.\n\n## Source checks\n\nChecked against upstream main `dc5a34dd1d2e60cadc20abb1523d0f5956f37487`:\n\n- `crates/app/src/mcp/tools.rs`: registry, import schema and dispatch.\n- `crates/app/src/mcp/units_tools.rs` and `commands/set_units.rs`: syntax, refusals and history.\n- `crates/app/src/units.rs`: internal metric dimensions and the display lens.\n- `crates/app/src/mcp/job.rs`: units, machine and setup-post fields.\n- `crates/app/src/script/api.rs`: re-import budget and import history.\n- `crates/app/src/geometry/import/step_budget.rs`, `import/mod.rs` and `commands/import_model.rs`: budget default, validation and recording.\n\n## Checks and limits\n\n- PASS: `python3 -m unittest discover -s .claude/skills/camcraft-mcp/tests -v` — 11 tests.\n- Regression proof: the new file runs four tests against the old skill. Three test methods fail on the missing entries; the existing-row check passes.\n- PASS: `git diff --check` and `git diff --cached --check` before commit.\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main` — zero selected steps. No Rust tests ran; this is not a Rust test pass.\n- NOT RUN: `cargo xtask gate light`. Its dry-run selects 11 light twins across six steps. The first step builds `camcraft-motion` and `camcraft-app` test targets in release mode. This documentation-only contribution has an explicit no-release-rebuild scope.\n- No example catalog, broad Rust suite, GUI or physical-machine checks ran. No runtime safety claim is made.\n\n## Process\n\nProcess change: yes\n\nThe current `AGENTS.md` assigns the process-version bump and #681 announcement to the merging session.\nThis PR does not change `.claude/PROCESS_VERSION`, despite the issue's older wording.\n\nEffort: low\n\nChangelog: none\n\nFixes #962\n",
